      <text xml:space="preserve">[[image:MarlineSpikeHitch.jpg|thumb|Marlinespike hitch]]
'''Canonical Name:''' marlinespike hitch.&lt;BR&gt;
'''Variant Name(s):''' None.&lt;BR&gt;
'''Category:''' Hitch.&lt;BR&gt;
'''Origin:''' Ancient.&lt;BR&gt;
'''Similarities:''' This knot is based on the overhand slipped knot&lt;BR&gt;
'''Releasing:''' Non-jamming, spills completely when the spike is removed&lt;BR&gt;
'''Efficiency:''' Unknown%.&lt;BR&gt;
'''Caveat:''' Spills.&lt;BR&gt;
'''Uses:''' Sailing or heaving on any line.&lt;BR&gt;
'''Comments:'''&lt;BR&gt;
'''Structure:'''&lt;BR&gt;
'''Tying:''' Create a slipped overhand on the standing end and place a spike through the slipped loop.&lt;BR&gt;

==See also==
* [[List of knots]]

