  <page>
    <title>Guignol</title>
    <id>56571</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41409381</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-27T03:21:12Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>24.255.24.70</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Guignol''' is a [[France|French]] [[puppet]] show for children. 

The character of ''Guignol'' was devised between [[1810]] and [[1812]] by Laurent Mourguet, an unemployed workman from [[Lyon]], supposedly in his own image. The man Laurent Mourguet was originally a silk weaver, but because of a lack of money became a dentist. He would travel from place to place pulling teeth with his large pincers, and eventually th people became scared of him, after hearing the screams of those having their teeth pulled, and would hide from him. To solve this, he created a puppet in his likeness to tell funny stories and ease people's fear of him. The puppet became so popular he stopped being a dentist completely and became a renowned puppeteer. The idea  caught on, and there were many Guignol shows (similar to the English 'Punch and Judy' shows that were satirical, and used to complain about God, the lords, King, and anyone the people had any grievances about) around France. The government was very afraid of these gatherings, and made puppet shows illegal, which just encouraged the shows more. Puppeteers would just setup shop in the middle                 
of a marketplace and move on when they were done. 

'''Guignol''' has a friend, '''Gnafron''', and an opponent, the '''[[Gendarme]] Flageolet'''

==See also==
* [[Les Guignols de l'Info]]

==External links==
* http://www.sagecraft.com/puppetry/performance/ltg/
* http://guignolsland.free.fr/w-guignol.html

[[fr:Guignol]]
[[de:Guignol]]

[[Category:Puppetry]]
[[Category:Lyon]]

==The band==

Guignol is also the name of a Brooklyn based punky Klezmer Quarter. Consisting of:
Franz Nicolay - Accordian
Peter Hess - Clarinet
George Rush - Tuba
John Bollinger - Drums

They are quickly making a name for themselves in the NYC based Gypsy-Punk scene. Guignol contains several members from [[The World/Inferno Friendship Society]] and [[Nanuchka]], and the bands share a slightly overlapping fanbase.

Releases:
Guignol (Self-titled) CD (2004) on Third Story Records
Drink the Best Wine First EP (Split w/ Nanuchka. Features Yula Be'eri on guest vocals)</text>
    </revision>
