      <text xml:space="preserve">{{For|the town in France|Castries, Hérault}}
{{For|the Saint Lucian Quarter of the same name|Castries Quarter}}

[[image:Santa lucia castries political.png|thumb|right|The Quarter of Castries, showing Castries city (red dot)]]
'''Castries''', population 11,147 ([[1991]]), is the capital city of [[Saint Lucia]].    [[West Indies]].  Castries is located at {{coor dm|14|1|N|60|59|W|}}. 


==History==
Castries was founded by the [[France|French]] in [[1650]], named after [[Charles Eugène Gabriel de la Croix, Marquis de Castries]]. Having previously been called &quot;Carenage&quot; (meaning safe anchorage).

Castries has been rebuilt, having been destroyed by fire several times, notably on [[June 19]], [[1948]].

==Tourism==
Castries is a port of call for cruise ships.

==Airports==  
Castries is served by [[George F. L. Charles Airport]]. Passengers on longer flights arrive at [[Hewanorra International Airport]], near [[Vieux-Fort]].

==Regional Institutions==
As well as being the capital city of Saint Lucia, Castries hosts the secretariat of the [[Organisation of Eastern Caribbean States]].

Castries also hosts the headquarters of the [[Eastern Caribbean Supreme Court]].

==See also==
*[[Organisation of Eastern Caribbean States]]
*[[Eastern Caribbean Supreme Court]]

==External links==
http://www.brigandhill.com/other.html


[[Category:Capitals in North America]]
[[Category:Saint Lucia]]


