  <page>
    <title>Cotonou</title>
    <id>56647</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41030207</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-24T16:30:02Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>DabMachine</username>
        <id>922466</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>disambiguation from [[Oil]] to [[Petroleum]] - ([[WP:DPL|You can help!]])</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:BJ-Cotonou.png|right|140px|Location of Cotonou in Benin]]
'''Cotonou''', population 536,827 ([[1992]]), is the seat of government of [[Benin]], though the official [[capital]] is [[Porto-Novo]]. Cotonou's [[airport]] and roads and rail facilities make it the transportation and communications hub of the country. Cotonou is located at 6&amp;deg;22' North, 2&amp;deg;26' East (6.36667, 2.4333). [http://earth-info.nga.mil/gns/html/cntry_files.html]

The city lies in the south east of the country, between the [[Atlantic Ocean]] and [[Nokoué Lake]], around the [[Cotonou Lagoon]] (actually a [[strait]]).

The city is best known as a major [[port]], and is also home to an [[airport]] and a [[railway]] to [[Parakou]].  Features of Cotonou include [[Cotonou Friendship Stadium]], [[Cotonou Cathedral]], [[Cotonou Central Mosque]] and [[Dantokpa Market]], which includes a [[fetish market]]. The [[National University of Benin]] is located in Cotonou.

Manufactures include [[palm oil]] and [[palm cake|cake]], [[brewing]], [[textiles]], and [[cement]].  [[automobile|Motor vehicles]] and [[bicycle]]s are assembled, and there are [[sawmill]]s in the city.  [[petroleum|Petroleum]] products, [[bauxite]] and [[iron]] are exported. Offshore drilling for [[Petroleum|oil]] is carried on.

Cotonou was originally dominated by the Kingdom of [[Dahomey]] from the [[18th century]].  In [[1851]] the [[France|French]] made a treaty with the Dahomean King [[Gezo]] that allowed them to establish a trading post at Cotonou.  In [[1883]] the French navy occupied the city to prevent [[United Kingdom|British]] conquest of the area.

==See also==
[[Cotonou Agreement]]

