      <comment>Grammatical correction ~~</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Satelite image of Malta.jpg|thumb|200px|Satellite image of Malta]]
[[Image:Map of Malta 2.png|right|200px| ]] 
[[Image:Mt-map.png|right|Map of Malta]]
The '''Geography of Malta''' is dominated by [[water]]. It is an [[archipelago]] of [[coralline limestone]], located in the [[Mediterranean Sea]], [[1 E5 m|~93&amp;nbsp;km]] south of [[Sicily]], [[Italy]], [[Europe]]; and ~300km north of [[Africa]]. Only the three largest islands [[Malta Island|Malta]], [[Gozo Island|Gozo]], and [[Comino Island|Comino]] are inhabited. The country is ~316 km&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; in area. Numerous [[Headlands and bays|bay]]s along the indented coastline of the [[island]]s provide good [[harbour]]s. The landscape of the islands is characterised by low hills with terraced fields. The highest point, at 253 [[metre|m]], is the [[Ta' Dmejrek]] on [[Malta Island]]. The capital is ''[[Valletta]]''. 

'''[[Geographic coordinates]]:'''
{{coor dm|35|50|N|14|35|E|type:country}}

'''Map references:'''
Europe

'''Area:'''
&lt;br&gt;''total:''
316 km²
&lt;br&gt;''land:''
316 km²
&lt;br&gt;''water:''
0 km²

'''Area - comparative:'''
slightly less than twice the size of Washington, DC

