      <comment>Disambiguate [[Richard Wright]] to [[Richard Wright (musician)]] using [[:en:Wikipedia:Tools/Navigation_popups|popups]]</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">A '''keyboardist''' is a [[musician]] who plays [[keyboard instrument]]s. In the early [[1960s]] musicians who played keyboards were generally classified as either [[piano|pianists]] or [[organ (music)|organists]].  Since the mid 1960s, a plethora of new musical instruments with keyboards have come into common usage, requiring a more general term for a person who plays them. These keyboards include:

*[[electric piano]]s such as the [[Fender Rhodes]] and [[Wurlitzer electric piano]]
*[[electronic piano]]s such as the [[Roland]] Digital Piano
*[[Hammond organ]]
*[[analog synthesizer]]s such as [[Moog synthesizer]] and [[Arp]] synthesizers
*[[digital synthesizer]]s such as those produced today by [[Roland]], [[Yamaha Corporation|Yamaha]] and [[Korg]]
*[[sampler]]s
*[[mellotron]]
*[[clavinet]]
*[[pianet]]
*[[piano]]
*[[harpsichord]]
*[[celeste]]
*[[clavichord]]
*[[pipe organ]]

==Notable keyboardists==

Note: this section lists people who predominantly played electric keyboards as detailed above. 

