    <title>Clarinetist</title>
    <id>56714</id>
    <revision>
      <id>42048836</id>
      <timestamp>2006-03-03T13:10:16Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Dompassmore</username>
        <id>1023041</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* [[European classical music|Classical]] */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">A '''clarinetist''' (sometimes also spelled '''clarinettist''') is a [[musician]] who plays the [[clarinet]]. Some clarinetists also play other woodwind instruments, particularly commonly the [[saxophone]], and may therefore also be [[saxophonist]]s and [[multireedist]]s.

Here is a list of famous clarinetists, grouped according to the musical idiom with which they are particularly associated.

''See also'' the Wikipedia [[:Category:Clarinetists]]

== [[European classical music|Classical]]==


* [[Mihajlo Avramović]](1937-2004),[[School of Music &quot;Stevan Hristić&quot;,Kruševac]],Serbia&amp;Montenegro
* [[Ernest Ačkun]]
* [[Scott Andrews]] Saint Louis Symphony Orchestra
* [[Laura Ardan]] Atlanta Symphony Orchestra
* [[Heinrich Bärmann]] Weber's clarinetist
* [[Cristro Barrios]]
* [[Mate Bekavac]],Berlin Philharmonic Orchestra[http://sl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mate_Bekavac]
* [[Rudolf Beran]]
* [[Julian Bliss]]
* [[David Blumberg http://www.mytempo.com]] Clarinetist / Producer
* [[Daniel Bonade]] Famed player in Stokowski's Philadelphia Orchestra
* [[Bruno Brun]]
* [[Jack Brymer]]
* [http://www.gamisim.com/artist/campbell/ James Campbell]
* [[Louis Cahuzac]] also a composer
* [[Ernesto Cavallini]] Classical virtuoso who worked with Verdi
* [[Franklin Cohen]] Cleveland Orchestra
* [[Michael Collins (musician)|Michael Collins]]
* [[Larry Combs]] Chicago Symphony
* [[Vladimir Cvija]]
* [[Tonči Djuka]]
* [[Stanley Drucker]] New York Philharmonic
* [[Anton Eberst]]
